swer-field/key "$\\text{nullity}(A)=5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673428} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08e87190-2841-5611-9c70-dc6033a40400" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673408} {:answer/id #uuid "d0b668ec-e524-508e-93cd-8eb84b3df602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673447}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673408} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1c24042-b870-5f0a-80ac-f4818e90caf5" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $5$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{5}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673435} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2390ff3f-82fc-54bf-9b85-5082cf00aedd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673414} {:answer/id #uuid "2b01ce81-b96e-5329-acb7-60b29187eee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673415}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673414} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba2b51a4-1c12-534c-8dce-a26aa8889459" :answer-field/key "$A$ is invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673442}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "01c27acc-5739-59f4-8fe9-e2185b961d5f" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix which has only $5$ non-pivot column?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible\n\n$$\n\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{5} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=5=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nThe 5 non-pivot columns give $\\text{nullity}(A)=5.$\n\nBy the rank-nullity theorem,\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+5=5,\\qquad \\text{rank}(A)=5-5=0.\n$$\n\nHence $\\text{rank}(A)=0$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=5$. Since rank is less than the number of columns, $A$ is not invertible and $\\det(A)=0$. Also, $\\text{Col}(A)$ has dimension 0. The number of pivot columns is 0, and the number of non-pivot columns is 5.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is invertible” is false. The rank is less than the number of columns.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $5$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{5}.$” is false. $\\dim(\\text{Col}(A))=0$.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{nullity}(A)=5$” is true. $\\text{nullity}(A)=5$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{nullity}(A)=5$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673411 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "366e42cb-2574-576c-ae6c-5df19e16a5c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673418} {:answer/id #uuid "b1b4a4ea-a7da-5796-ba31-4f54586baecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673439}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673439} :answer-field/id #uuid "1aff7ca8-ae95-5320-870a-283e02efa317" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673412} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34b9502c-410e-52f5-b026-c2f9b31705b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673417} {:answer/id #uuid "a1dc0d68-471b-5062-b20b-5752e4b0dd3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673436}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673436} :answer-field/id #uuid "49d0098d-44ad-5e1e-85dd-1dbbc7334091" :answer-field/key "$\\text{nullity}(A)=8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673421} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9efa1286-95cb-5e3d-9779-3876fa3adc06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673434} {:answer/id #uuid "c8a03354-d256-5b30-83a7-5851e5a7b6ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673445}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673434} :answer-field/id #uuid "68418815-8305-5b5e-9da2-656a31ba6134" :answer-field/key "$A$ is invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1a6f89b5-17bd-5c0c-b910-92e1887d4880" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $10\\times 10$ matrix with $2$ pivot columns?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $10\\times 10$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible\n\n$$\n\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{10} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=10=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nThe 2 pivot columns give $\\text{rank}(A)=2.$\n\nBy the rank-nullity theorem,\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n$$\n2+\\text{nullity}(A)=10,\\qquad \\text{nullity}(A)=10-2=8.\n$$\n\nHence $\\text{rank}(A)=2$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=8$. Since rank is less than the number of columns, $A$ is not invertible and $\\det(A)=0$. Also, $\\text{Col}(A)$ has dimension 2. The number of pivot columns is 2, and the number of non-pivot columns is 8.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is invertible” is false. The rank is less than the number of columns.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{nullity}(A)=8$” is true. $\\text{nullity}(A)=8$.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{rank}(A)=2$” is true. $\\text{rank}(A)=2$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{nullity}(A)=8$; $\\text{rank}(A)=2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673413 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12f8229f-ef39-5cfa-a4bd-a0f2f936e940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673410} {:answer/id #uuid "47514b44-7fec-5627-8a5b-bcce4012cc85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673420} {:answer/id #uuid "a327f0df-7451-5065-ba8a-d07d7567aa5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673437} {:answer/id #uuid "d8369a5b-132b-5815-ac55-3ca829df5152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673449} {:answer/id #uuid "de9acc3e-1ada-5d6a-9abe-29947f31aa9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673450}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673420} :answer-field/id #uuid "08b95a80-6d17-56c6-be43-c7d7451f84eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673407}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1c93f8c9-c546-50e4-a1df-c54e8f82f0eb" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix with $3$ pivot columns?\n\nI. $\\text{rank}(A)=5$\n\nII. $A$ is not invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{nullity}(A)=1$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{8} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=8=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nThe 3 pivot columns give $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$\n\nBy the rank-nullity theorem,\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n$$\n3+\\text{nullity}(A)=8,\\qquad \\text{nullity}(A)=8-3=5.\n$$\n\nHence $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=5$. Since rank is less than the number of columns, $A$ is not invertible and $\\det(A)=0$. Also, $\\text{Col}(A)$ has dimension 3. The number of pivot columns is 3, and the number of non-pivot columns is 5.\n\n- Statement I is false. $\\text{rank}(A)=3$.\n\n- Statement II is true. The rank is less than the number of columns.\n\n- Statement III is false. $\\text{nullity}(A)=5$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is II only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673426 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cd61621-e086-56a9-ae64-6d28ed6d1944" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673427} {:answer/id #uuid "8ad663d6-03d5-593b-8d23-be79be698d83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673432}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673432} :answer-field/id #uuid "54107d25-70b8-589c-83d0-fde2f4e5a0fb" :answer-field/key "$A$ is not invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673424} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12d11e7b-2e35-5882-ae11-4fee9d03b2dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673409} {:answer/id #uuid "f27e0ecc-9ad0-52b4-9fc9-97c1ee550c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673451}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673451} :answer-field/id #uuid "a989528a-e5a8-5859-bd54-1f3759ea645b" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673438} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c3b4623-c248-5a02-b8ee-7ba16209f579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673416} {:answer/id #uuid "bd48ae13-0ac2-55cd-85b8-8715b9df1712" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673444}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673416} :answer-field/id #uuid "b207d561-698d-59e0-a012-bb9ff356ca43" :answer-field/key "$det(A)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5b807f80-d3e7-5284-9d78-b367cb5db361" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and  $\\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2a \\\\ 3a \\\\ 3b\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,a,b\\in R\\right\\}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible\n\n$$\n\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{3} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=3=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$  \n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nThe supplied null space has the independent spanning vectors\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThus $\\text{nullity}(A)=2.$\n\nBy the rank-nullity theorem,\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+2=3,\\qquad \\text{rank}(A)=3-2=1.\n$$\n\nHence $\\text{rank}(A)=1$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=2$. Since rank is less than the number of columns, $A$ is not invertible and $\\det(A)=0$. Also, $\\text{Col}(A)$ has dimension 1. The number of pivot columns is 1, and the number of non-pivot columns is 2.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is not invertible” is true. The rank is less than the number of columns.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{rank}(A)=0$” is false. $\\text{rank}(A)=1$.\n\n- Statement “$det(A)=0$” is true. $A$ is not invertible, so $\\det(A)=0$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A$ is not invertible; $det(A)=0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673452 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bf661d7-522d-523e-924c-cf70e56ef4c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673422} {:answer/id #uuid "50595a0f-e68c-5eb9-8d4e-509557233567" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673423}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673422} :answer-field/id #uuid "56e65182-7ecd-5970-9716-4a82b7f451d7" :answer-field/key "$A$ is not invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673425} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7cdb4946-a773-51de-8878-8b57d29bd2a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673430} {:answer/id #uuid "8e4ad4a5-953b-533a-8148-f2399789ddb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673433}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673430} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e9d96e5-a8d2-524c-9ca1-ee4d9e72432e" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $3$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{7}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673431} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb6ddb6a-a2fb-5bdc-afea-25f9024d2e18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673443} {:answer/id #uuid "cba8c704-e212-5518-be74-5971633bb01d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673446}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673443} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5ec3bf1-9be3-5daa-bfbb-855721c618f1" :answer-field/key "$\\text{nullity}(A)=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f7fdbf75-0d39-5481-92c5-3bb3459c2aeb" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix which has only $2$ non-pivot column?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible\n\n$$\n\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{7} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=7=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nThe 2 non-pivot columns give $\\text{nullity}(A)=2.$\n\nBy the rank-nullity theorem,\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+2=7,\\qquad \\text{rank}(A)=7-2=5.\n$$\n\nHence $\\text{rank}(A)=5$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=2$. Since rank is less than the number of columns, $A$ is not invertible and $\\det(A)=0$. Also, $\\text{Col}(A)$ has dimension 5. The number of pivot columns is 5, and the number of non-pivot columns is 2.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is not invertible” is true. The rank is less than the number of columns.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $3$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{7}.$” is false. $\\dim(\\text{Col}(A))=5$.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{nullity}(A)=2$” is true. $\\text{nullity}(A)=2$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A$ is not invertible; $\\text{nullity}(A)=2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673956 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "222d2288-8ec8-5e6d-a4d8-095077c48bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673946} {:answer/id #uuid "6aee5c58-e2b4-5f01-b8e0-82c1d4d6fae3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673957} {:answer/id #uuid "c538572d-fdb5-5531-91f3-68a9da295fe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673971} {:answer/id #uuid "dbfaa07e-0f58-59c2-893c-21f92247653a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673974} {:answer/id #uuid "fe4de40d-50a1-5d55-88c4-b30849d049d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673976}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673971} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3f58f00-49ce-5578-a2fd-f96ec70eeb0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673969}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6a93d453-0c6e-55ff-bedb-71deca93f8cf" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y &=-3 \\\\ 2x+ky &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & k & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & k & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & k+8 & 10\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y &=-3 \\\\ (k+8)y &=10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-8,$ then the second equation is $0=10,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673961 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1efe90b4-562a-5953-a6a1-cc05ec46980b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673943} {:answer/id #uuid "67823551-800c-5cf7-948d-beb12cd02bf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673955} {:answer/id #uuid "8b8fa752-119c-51a0-b6e2-66d7985075e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673963} {:answer/id #uuid "98c304e3-a115-5ace-9fab-90964849999e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673965} {:answer/id #uuid "c4f936e8-86b0-5f40-9374-4f0caee0a413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673970}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673965} :answer-field/id #uuid "65831a37-c7e4-528e-a925-5b3e241729ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "81014666-3726-55af-9dd0-135ed4dcb4b9" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-2 \\\\ -2x+ky &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & k & -8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & k & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & k-4 & -12\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-2 \\\\ (k-4)y &=-12.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=4,$ then the second equation is $0=-12,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25a84b70-9245-5d97-a4d9-55045854331f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673947} {:answer/id #uuid "2d9d77cc-bf23-57d7-922e-1fb20688eb3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673948} {:answer/id #uuid "4116de3c-ec2b-537f-a54c-e14f8c2d7871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673952} {:answer/id #uuid "879ad630-9d2f-568c-8679-659f0ddc56fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673962} {:answer/id #uuid "c3161b92-ed93-588e-b5d8-221d41adb4bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673968}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673947} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ee32c4a-a732-5943-9bdb-dec719ab233a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8ed86d41-824a-5162-a0b1-66e0498bfd9d" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y &=-3 \\\\ 3x+ky &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 3 & k & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 3 & k & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & k+12 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y &=-3 \\\\ (k+12)y &=9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-12,$ then the second equation is $0=9,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673966 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "044d5930-e9c2-5606-a6c3-a9b35fdcaf64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673942} {:answer/id #uuid "1fb6ed59-3b1b-5e76-8348-af3553644638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673944} {:answer/id #uuid "3fb5c6d1-171c-5fac-96b5-ed6bc2cb9d60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673951} {:answer/id #uuid "483b361a-fa4f-569e-9ee3-9a27510e751b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673953} {:answer/id #uuid "f0daf48f-38d9-5ace-b9ce-998b60036b8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "k=11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673975}] :an