egin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $BC$, the entry in row $2$, column $1$ is $2$, whereas the identity entry is $0$. This mismatch proves that $C$ is not an inverse of $B$. One failing product suffices to reject the pair.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA&=\\begin{bmatrix}1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot (-2) & 1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1 \\\\ 2\\cdot 1+0\\cdot (-2) & 2\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $BA$, the entry in row $2$, column $1$ is $2$, whereas the identity entry is $0$. This mismatch proves that $A$ is not an inverse of $B$. One failing product suffices to reject the pair.\n\nThe statement $A$ is an inverse of $C$ is **true**.\n\nThe statement $BC=CB=I_2$ is **false**.\n\nThe statement $BA=AB=I_2$ is **false**.\n\nSelect $A$ is an inverse of $C$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699332 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43031476-f7f8-5d71-8754-aebfc44341ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699307} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ac89ba-f077-5177-adb1-057312896b04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699334}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699307} :answer-field/id #uuid "069855c5-00e3-501c-94bd-675a0db209b0" :answer-field/key "$B$ is not an inverse of $C$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699294} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53687a2b-2a3a-534a-a2ca-087fd8f9bea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699308} {:answer/id #uuid "d558c9b6-5196-5d03-af14-1083c45215ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699340}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699308} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ad8127a-903f-5525-ba66-bed783f69c2d" :answer-field/key "$AB=BA=I_2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699300} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cd52aa4-7d02-51c9-9cbf-16b1042e0bcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699315} {:answer/id #uuid "7b4c23c0-df14-5c17-a608-8078f4c6c15a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699317}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699317} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c3902df-44ae-55fb-b4a3-5e74647f218e" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699314} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c203871-549f-557c-9405-17b249534972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699301} {:answer/id #uuid "cf92186c-3b0d-5e4c-acb3-5ff89314bc55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699338}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699338} :answer-field/id #uuid "a81d8818-cb8c-518d-afb2-dd12c47db856" :answer-field/key "$AC=CA=I_2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b140ed22-3eb8-5900-8ef2-9abaa992b4ca" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRecall that two matrices are inverses when their products in both orders equal $I_2$.\n\nWhich statements are true? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Use row-column multiplication and compare with $I_2$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB&=\\begin{bmatrix}(-1)\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0 & (-1)\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 1\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0 & 1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $AB$, the entry in row $1$, column $1$ is $-1$, whereas the identity entry is $1$. This mismatch proves that $B$ is not an inverse of $A$. One failing product suffices to reject the pair.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC&=\\begin{bmatrix}(-1)\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0 & (-1)\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot 1 \\\\ 1\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0 & 1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $AC$, the entry in row $1$, column $1$ is $-1$, whereas the identity entry is $1$. This mismatch proves that $C$ is not an inverse of $A$. One failing product suffices to reject the pair.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CB&=\\begin{bmatrix}1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0 & 1\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 0 \\\\ 0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0 & 0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $CB$, the entry in row $2$, column $2$ is $0$, whereas the identity entry is $1$. This mismatch proves that $B$ is not an inverse of $C$. One failing product suffices to reject the pair.\n\nThe statement $AB=BA=I_2$ is **false**.\n\nThe statement $AC=CA=I_2$ is **false**.\n\nThe statement $B$ is not an inverse of $C$ is **true**. It negates the inverse relationship.\n\nSelect $B$ is not an inverse of $C$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699343 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36d952e9-59db-504f-88ed-33a8fb373615" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699303} {:answer/id #uuid "8b0caaf6-fa36-5760-857d-ed95f69ca8e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699324} {:answer/id #uuid "97122257-900b-5a5c-951d-241bb499c473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699326} {:answer/id #uuid "bafc2079-4893-5538-8804-d4e97fc5c7e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699335} {:answer/id #uuid "bc067d53-049c-5abe-a6c5-c63efc8029e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699336}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699326} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9dc3a84-0441-5e39-b979-2ab832d1eef8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699344}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e5066df1-b3fb-575a-b992-3b42a1a41712" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRecall that two matrices are inverses when their products in both orders equal $I_2$.\n\nWhich statements are true? Choose the correct combination.\n\nI. $BC=CB=I_2$\n\nII. $BA=AB=I_2$\n\nIII. $A$ is an inverse of $C$" :question/worked-solution "Use row-column multiplication and compare with $I_2$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC&=\\begin{bmatrix}0\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 2 & 0\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1 \\\\ 0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 2 & 0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $BC$, the entry in row $1$, column $1$ is $0$, whereas the identity entry is $1$. This mismatch proves that $C$ is not an inverse of $B$. One failing product suffices to reject the pair.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA&=\\begin{bmatrix}0\\cdot 1+0\\cdot (-2) & 0\\cdot 1+0\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-2) & 0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $BA$, the entry in row $1$, column $1$ is $0$, whereas the identity entry is $1$. This mismatch proves that $A$ is not an inverse of $B$. One failing product suffices to reject the pair.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA&=\\begin{bmatrix}1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot (-2) & 1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-2) & 2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $CA$, the entry in row $1$, column $2$ is $1$, whereas the identity entry is $0$. This mismatch proves that $A$ is not an inverse of $C$. One failing product suffices to reject the pair.\n\nThe statement $BC=CB=I_2$ is **false**.\n\nThe statement $BA=AB=I_2$ is **false**.\n\nThe statement $A$ is an inverse of $C$ is **false**.\n\nThe correct combination is None."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699366 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13d502e0-020d-5dfd-a7e2-19eccdb27732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699350} {:answer/id #uuid "6f7706b0-f1c9-50f0-9f7b-273d4f5b8058" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699371}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699350} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a0e7930-59b8-57b1-a8f4-719a93eb771d" :answer-field/key "$BC=CB=I_3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699349} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a7dc66c-3198-5852-baa4-20d28838d709" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699382} {:answer/id #uuid "f3c75e12-0c43-5c55-8bdd-c402d194feb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699407}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699407} :answer-field/id #uuid "25a16fa3-8726-50e0-b3b8-8a08b1dc39e5" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699356} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42acf297-e0d4-5c42-a297-3daab72d4d38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699363} {:answer/id #uuid "7f115a4d-032a-5a35-988f-4ebc12f63375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699375}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699375} :answer-field/id #uuid "987ad129-be0f-51a6-83ea-26af623a6570" :answer-field/key "$C\\ne B^{-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699381} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02ae4d43-617f-5855-ac9b-98020ace2a72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699347} {:answer/id #uuid "d1fbe26d-cc5e-5d78-be83-6aa709600993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699397}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699397} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0433d89-afac-5369-ab18-d8c05e5b5764" :answer-field/key "$BA=AB=I_3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4fa2286b-367e-557c-b593-764f80dc030f" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\frac{1}{28}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -6 & -2 \\\\ -14 & -34 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\frac{1}{14}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -12 & -4 \\\\ -28 & -68 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -16 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true? Use direct verification.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "In the products below, each outside scalar has been distributed across its matrix entries.\n\nCheck $C$. The entry in row $1$, column $1$ already disproves the identity claim:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(BC)_{11}&=(3)(0)+(-1)(-2)+(2)(0) \\\\ &=2\\ne 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $BC\\ne I_3$, so $C$ is not an inverse of $B$. One mismatching entry is enough to reject a candidate.\n\nCheck $A$. The entry in row $1$, column $1$ already disproves the identity claim:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(BA)_{11}&=(3)(0)+(-1)\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+(2)(0) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2}\\ne 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $BA\\ne I_3$, so $A$ is not an inverse of $B$. One mismatching entry is enough to reject a candidate.\n\nThe statement $C\\ne B^{-1}$ is **true** by the product test above.\n\nSelect $C\\ne B^{-1}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699370 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d507161-e2bc-515a-a6e0-531b9725cdcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699384} {:answer/id #uuid "d5ac562a-04f8-5b7f-bcdb-c980ebd5bcb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699399}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699384} :answer-field/id #uuid "89cb22d7-0036-5005-bcc5-dedaa36b5c23" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699377} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ff28464-e969-5b2f-9bee-2e2e487de9ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699362} {:answer/id #uuid "443cfb48-4b10-572e-a3a7-ac20fc0287ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699364}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699362} :answer-field/id #uuid "c506859b-2a48-5dc7-84de-eb94953b10ee" :answer-field/key "$BC=CB=I_3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699390} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f84d7f9-46c7-5cd1-b7cd-9e6f53563248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699352} {:answer/id #uuid "8fe58a3a-f0cc-5a8b-a05e-fe54aedafbcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699380}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699352} :answer-field/id #uuid "e22ec1a2-2608-5b26-aab4-92a55e2e6200" :answer-field/key "$C=B^{-1}$" :answer-field/type 